<LegalLayout title="Accessibility statement | AImpetus" heading="Accessibility statement">
  <p class="lede">We want everyone to be able to use aimpetus.ai, including people who use assistive technology. Many of the organisations we work with have to meet public-sector accessibility standards, and we hold our own website to the same standard.</p>

  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. That means you should be able to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>navigate the whole site using just a keyboard</li>
    <li>use the site with a screen reader</li>
    <li>zoom in up to 400% without text spilling off the screen</li>
    <li>change colours, contrast and fonts using your browser or device settings</li>
    <li>read text that meets AA colour contrast</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How accessible this website is</h2>
  <p>We last tested the site on <Placeholder text="test date" /> using <Placeholder text="method, for example automated checks and manual keyboard and screen reader testing" />.</p>
  <p><Placeholder text={'either "We are not aware of any accessibility problems" or a short list of known issues and when we plan to fix them.'} /></p>

  <h2>Feedback and contact</h2>
  <p>If you find a problem, or need information in a different format, email <a href="mailto:contact@aimpetus.ai">contact@aimpetus.ai</a>. Tell us the page and what went wrong. We'll reply within 5 working days.</p>

  <h2>Keeping this up to date</h2>
  <p>We review this statement whenever we make significant changes to the site, and at least once a year.</p>
</LegalLayout>
